9. The database file is in an instance/ folder. Why do you think Flask puts it there instead of the root folder?
Flask puts the database file in the instance/ folder because that folder is meant for data that changes and should not be part of the main codebase. The instance/ folder is not tracked by Git by default, which prevents a sensitive files like the SQLite database from being committed. It also keeps the database safe during updates, since the root folder might change but the instance/ folder stays persistent.

